fact WorkItem(id: "WI-268", description: some(value: "Document entity ↔ term runtime mapping in docs/design/. Five load-bearing rules across the entity-term boundary live only in inline code comments today and bit cmd_X (WI-267) hard during port: (1) Value::Entity → Term::Fn lowering (kb/execute.rs alloc_from_value): recursive field allocation, named_args sorted to declaration order. (2) Term::Fn → Value::Entity materialization (eval/builtins.rs materialize_entity / term_as_entity): walks entity_field_types, finds value in named_args or pos_args by index, defaults missing Option-typed fields to none(), recurses via term_to_value; treats Var-valued Option fields as semantically absent (WI-267 fix). (3) Loader partial-named-arg expansion (kb/load.rs:2752 + :3492): every absent named slot gets fresh_var(field_name) stuffed in so the discrim tree can index uniformly; positional args count as provided (WI-267 fix). (4) Printer 0-arg Fn ↔ Ref round-trip asymmetry (persistence/print.rs): Fn(X, []) prints as bare 'X' (no parens), parser loads back as Term::Ref(X) — pattern matcher now accepts Ref/Ident as 0-arg Fn (WI-267 fix). (5) is_option_type peels Type entity wrapper — load_entity stores field types as parameterized(base: sort_ref(name: Option), ...) not bare Option (WI-267 fix). Acceptance: docs/design/entity-term-mapping.md exists, covers all five rules with examples (WorkItem fact load → materialize → with_X → alloc_from_value → persist round-trip), cross-links to the relevant source files; kernel-language.md §6.3 gets a 'see also' pointer. cargo test green. Driver: WI-267 spent ~half its time rediscovering these rules; future bundle authors should not pay that cost."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-267"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-13T17:48:54Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-268", author: "user", content: "Delivered: docs/design/entity-term-mapping.md — a compact reference for the five Value::Entity<->Term::Fn runtime rules (1 alloc_from_value lowering; 2 materialize_entity/term_to_value; 3 loader partial-named-arg expansion; 4 0-ary Ref canon; 5 is_option_type), plus a value-vs-pattern-position section, a worked WorkItem round-trip, and a file:line source-map table. Documented to HEAD (not frozen at WI-267): includes WI-500/WI-511 evolution. kernel-language.md §6.3 got a concise \"see also\" pointer, not a spec chapter — the mapping is internal-representation with no surface-language effect. Verified by independent source fact-checkers (every file:line citation exact; a few precision nits fixed) and cargo-test green. Rewritten compact per user preference (tables + one-liners over prose). NOTE: this doc's review is what surfaced the WI-716 optional-none-fill soundness bug.", at: "2026-07-13T17:48:55Z")
